ticle class="cap-card" id="cap-7"><div class="cap-img"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 4h16a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v12a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2z"/><polyline points="22,6 12,13 2,6"/></svg></div><div class="cap-body"><h3>CCM Migration &amp; Forms</h3><p class="lead">Migrate legacy Customer Communication Management to Quadient, without breaking carrier compliance.</p><ul><li>Legacy CCM platform discovery &amp; assessment</li><li>Form library inventory and mapping</li><li>Quadient template build-out and triggers</li><li>Integration with ClaimCenter and PolicyCenter</li><li>Regression testing and post-go-live support</li></ul><div class="proof">14 CCM programs · 13,000+ forms migrated to Quadient</div></div></article><article class="cap-card" id="cap-8"><div class="cap-img"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg></div><div class="cap-body"><h3>Workbench</h3><p class="lead">Configurable workbenches that extend Guidewire and lift productivity for claims handlers, underwriters, and agents.</p><ul><li>Claims handler workbenches</li><li>Underwriter workbenches</li><li>Agent and producer workbenches</li><li>Integrated with ClaimCenter &amp; PolicyCenter</li><li>AI-assisted productivity tools</li></ul><div class="proof">Workbenches built on real carrier workflows</div></div></article></div></div></section><section class="band a "><div class="container-fluid px-4"><div class="split-head"><h2 class="gw-section-title">The Current State of Guidewire Programs</h2><div class="lead-in"><strong>Why so many Guidewire programs stall, and what carriers are doing about it.</strong>Guidewire is the right platform. That is not the question. The question is why so many carriers are on their second or third Guidewire program, on the wrong release of Guidewire Cloud, or running an implementation that has slipped twice. Three industry-wide patterns explain most of it.</div></div><div class="challenges-grid"><article class="challenge"><div aria-hidden="true" class="ico"><svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg></div><h3>The multi-vendor failure pattern</h3><p>Too many carriers have lived through two or three system integrators on the same Guidewire program. Discovery slides become Build slips. Build slips become budget overruns. The carrier ends up paying for the same scope twice, once to the partner who failed it, once to the partner who recovers it.</p></article><article class="challenge"><div aria-hidden="true" class="ico"><svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2" y="2" width="20" height="8" rx="2"/><rect x="2" y="14" width="20" height="8" rx="2"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="6.01" y2="6"/><line x1="6" y1="18" x2="6.01" y2="18"/></svg></div><h3>Cloud migration treated as lift-and-shift</h3><p>The shift to Guidewire Cloud Platform, Palisades, Kufri, Jasper, is not a hosting change. It rewires how the carrier consumes releases, how integrations are built, and how regression discipline operates. Partners treating it as lift-and-shift miss the integration re-platforming and automation needed.</p></article><article class="challenge"><div aria-hidden="true" class="ico"><svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg></div><h3>Engineering capacity without domain depth</h3><p>Certified Guidewire engineers are scarce. Engineers who also understand P&amp;C, adjuster cycle time, claims leakage, underwriting referrals, regulatory reporting across 50 states, are scarcer still. Carriers feel the gap on the first design workshop, where business requirements meet platform configuration.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="band b "><div class="container-fluid px-4"><div class="split-head"><h2 class="gw-section-title">How Mahathi Helps</h2><div class="lead-in"><strong>How Mahathi helps insurers respond to these Guidewire challenges.</strong>Each challenge above has a practical response. Mahathi brings certified Guidewire capability, deep insurance domain knowledge, and delivery experience across 40+ Guidewire programs to help insurers move forward with confidence.</div></div><div class="solutions-grid" style="margin-bottom:56px"><article class="solution"><div class="sol-num">01</div><h3>Get your Guidewire program moving again.</h3><p class="sol-body">When a Guidewire program slows down or loses direction, Mahathi helps insurers get it back on track. The team starts with a focused assessment to understand what is causing the delay, and then delivers a clear plan with practical milestones until the program reaches working production.</p><div class="sol-proof"><span class="sol-proof-num">40+</span><span class="sol-proof-text">Guidewire programs delivered, including program recoveries</span></div></article><article class="solution"><div class="sol-num">02</div><h3>Move to Guidewire Cloud with confidence.</h3><p class="sol-body">Moving to Guidewire Cloud affects how a carrier consumes releases, manages integrations, and supports the platform every day. Mahathi helps insurers plan the move, prepare integrations, test thoroughly, and align with Guidewire Cloud release cycles, so the migration lands without disrupting the business.</p><div class="sol-proof"><span class="sol-proof-num">P·K·J</span><span class="sol-proof-text">Supported across Palisades, Kufri, and Jasper releases</span></div></article><article class="solution"><div class="sol-num">03</div><h3>Guidewire experts who understand your business.</h3><p class="sol-body">Mahathi pairs Guidewire-certified engineering with deep insurance domain knowledge in one team. With more than 80 Guidewire-certified resources and 350+ insurance domain professionals, the team understands both the platform and the insurance business it supports, so decisions match how insurers actually run their operations.</p><div class="sol-proof"><span class="sol-proof-num">80+ · 350+</span><span class="sol-proof-text">Certified resources and insurance domain experts</span></div></article></div><div class="sol-cta"><div class="sol-cta-text"><span class="sol-cta-eyebrow">Get in Touch</span><h3>Speak to our team</h3><p>Interested in learning more about our offerings? Our solutions specialists are ready to help.</p></div><a class="sol-cta-btn" href="<?= esc_url(mh_url('/contact-us')) ?>">Get in Touch <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/><polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19"/></svg></a></div></div></section><section class="band a faq-band"><div class="container-fluid px-4"><div class="faq-head"><h2 class="gw-section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><p>Guidewire, the questions carriers actually ask.</p></div><div class="faq-list">
